@startuml
title Current backend | Publish/edit gate | FR-005 / ADR-024/030
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #475569
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam activityBorderColor #475569
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam stateBorderColor #475569
actor "User acting as Teacher\naccount role=user" as U
participant Gateway as G
participant "Create / Update Class use case" as C
participant "assertPublishable policy" as P
database "live_class schema" as D
queue RabbitMQ as Q
participant "Shared consumer / ProjectTeacherTrustUseCase" as E
Q -> E: student.verification.* / skill.evidence.*
E -> D: Own-schema UPSERT teacher_verified / teacher_skill_approval\nApply only newer occurred_at; message deduplication
note over E,D: verified = status approved; missing rows deny publish.\nSkill approved event sets approvedLevel; other subscribed statuses clear it.\nProjection is eventually consistent; no cross-schema SELECT.
U -> G: POST /api/classes\nskillIds + schedule + price + capacity
G -> C: Authenticated user; trusted identity (not role=teacher)
C -> C: Validate duration, capacity, integer price and future start
C -> D: SqlTeacherTrustProjector.read(accountId)\nRead teacher_verified and teacher_skill_approval only
C -> P: assertPublishable(trust, skillIds)\nCurrent endpoint uses default requiredLevel=beginner
alt no skills / unverified / missing approval / level insufficient
 P --> C: Typed publish-gate error
 C --> U: Error mapped by domain-error filter; no class created
else every skill approved and student verified
 P --> C: Allowed
 C -> D: Persist Published class and class_skills
 C --> U: Class resource
end
opt PATCH /api/classes/:id
 U -> G: Class edit request
 G -> C: Current identity + changed fields
 C -> D: Read class; current Confirmed booking count
 C -> C: Check owner, nonterminal state, edit lock and future start
 opt skillIds supplied
  C -> D: Read current own-schema trust
  C -> P: Re-check every resulting skill
 end
 C -> D: Update class and skills
 C --> U: Updated class
end
note over U,C: Learner and Teacher are capabilities, not separate account roles.\nPublic registration creates user only; verifier/admin are provisioned.
@enduml
